  "notes": "Dark pro-tool look (zinc-gray surfaces) with a single amber accent #f5a524 used for primary buttons, active segmented items, active tool (Move outline), and the selected shot (1A). Emoji are used as icons throughout (🎬, 💃, asset tiles). Filmmaking vocabulary: spike-tape 'T' floor marks numbered 1-7, red dashed actor path, white dashed camera path, shot list with durations, lens/aspect HUD chips that cycle on click. Asset library is very long (People/Animals/Vehicles/Furniture 39/Props 86/Environments 55/Primitives) of 2-col emoji tiles. Modes STAGE/SHOOT/DELIVER: SHOOT (checked live) adds shot framing buttons (WS/FS/MS/MCU/CU, OTS, DUTCH), Record camera/performance, and a multi-track timeline with numbered mark pills per character — not in the capture. Help opens a modal with Quick start cards and a coach checklist. Proposed new entry scene-editor-3d since no 3D authoring pattern exists."
